            "{\r\n \"version\": 42,\r\n \"_repairCrystalCarveOutNote\": \"v42 = PROD-014 SLICE (d). OWNER RULING 2026-08-24 amends WO-947: regular structures are BUILT and UPGRADED with wood + iron and magical ones with crystals, but REPAIR may be paid in CRYSTALS for anything. OWNER RULING 2026-08-26 sets the rate: 1.0 CRYSTAL PER IRON -- 60% above the measured 0.625 natural-exchange floor (the $1.99 impulse rung), so a player who HAS iron still spends iron and crystals stay a convenience rather than a discount. It is authored as repo.repairCrystalsPer on the repair_default row and NOWHERE ELSE; CostBasketSeparationRegression [repair-carve-out] FAILS if a second row authors one, if the rate drops to or below the floor, or if repair pricing ever puts crystals into an ordinary basket. perWood/perFood are 0 = NOT CONVERTIBLE: no rate was ruled for them and inventing one would be economy policy, which is why this slice sat blocked. Bumping this file means CatalogFallbackData.g.cs MUST be regenerated (DeNelle.Editor.CatalogFallbackGenerator.Generate).\",\r\n \"_wo1082PaletteTailNote\": \"WO-1082 SECTION 4a (OWNER RULING 2026-08-26; 4b REJECTED): the barracks row moved ABOVE lumberyard so the three storage containers (lumberyard, foundry, silo) are the LAST Resource rows in entries[]. Nothing else moved - no id, no cost, no buildCost, no upgradeCost, no displayOrder, no lock state. 4b (moving the three collector_* rows to the end) was REJECTED because it requires deleting collector_lumbermill's displayOrder 10, which reverses the shipped WO-963 tutorial ruling that BuildCarouselTutorialOrderRegression case 2 protects. ARRAY POSITION IS ONLY HALF THE LEVER: BuildPaletteVM.AggregateOfType concatenates the verb's catalogTypes TYPE-MAJOR, so every Collector row trails every Resource row regardless of this file. The matching half is the Town row catalogTypes order in build-categories.json (see _wo1082TownTypeOrderNote there). Neither edit alone puts the containers last.\",\r\n \"_containerScaleNote2026_08_26\": \"WO-1224 Slice A: lumberyard, foundry and si",
            "lo share the wide GenericContainer art, which the owner measured on device as reading about twice town scale. All three author heightMul 0.5 as one family. Lowering the uniform fit shrinks both height and footprint and is save-overlap-safe; device felt-test owns the final visual dial. Slice B placeholder-art replacement remains blocked and is not part of this version.\",\r\n \"_rolePassNote2026_08_24\": \"WO-1167 grouped the Town palette by authored roles. mine_crystal is unlocked and its crystal_producer role belongs in the Producers group (WO-1081); mill and lumbermill remain locked legacy rows with unique roles. Role grouping remains data-authored, never a code map (WO-1161).\",\r\n \"_manageFilterNote2026_09_06\": \"WO-2005: manageFilters is the DATA authority for the Manage > BUILD filter chips (ALL / ECONOMY / DEFENSE / CRAFT / STORAGE). The UI must never infer a category from an id prefix, a class name, an asset name or a source tab (Manage redesign canon section 3). Legal tokens are pinned by DeNelle.Core.Catalog.BuildFilter; every row the build browser OFFERS must carry at least one. manageArtKey is the Sheet A tile name for this row (docs/ART_DELIVERY_2026-09-06_manage_assets.md appendix) - the art-name-to-catalog-id join lives HERE, in data, never in a resolver that parses names. Rows that are not player content (deco_torch, repair_default) carry neither.\",\r\n \"_sinkPassNote\": \"v24 = ECONOMY SINK PASS 2026-08-21 (OWNER RULING): a committed daily player should need 8-12 WEEKS to exhaust current content, a casual ~6 months; it was ONE EVENING. THE LEVER IS THE SINKS, NOT THE FAUCET -- harvest stays exactly 5 per 5 seconds (EchoBonusCalculator CommonResourcePerHour 3600) because \\\" 5 wood every 5 seconds\\\" is legible and a player can feel it; nudging it to 3.7/tick buys nothing and costs comprehension. Scaling factors: build x4, upgrade->L2 x10, upgrade->L3 x14. The THREE STORAGE ROWS (lumberyard/foundry/silo) use their own DECREASING ladder (x16/x16/x10/x8/x6.5/x6) because a uniform multiplier on a ladder that alread",
            "y doubles per step walks the cost off the end of the cap ladder it is gated behind -- foundry and silo wood steps were then lowered again by hand to 2000/2700/4000/6800/12000 because they are paid in WOOD, capped by the LUMBERYARD, and must fit the MATCHED container level. HARD CONSTRAINT, pinned by DeNelle.Editor.Regression.EconomySinkCapRegression [sink-cap]: NO COST MAY EXCEED THE MAX BANKABLE AMOUNT OF THAT RESOURCE (base 2000 + one container at level 1..6 = 3k/4k/6k/10k/18k/34k). A 3000-wood cost under a 2000 cap is UNCOMPLETABLE and nothing in the game explains why. CRYSTALS AND COINS ARE UNCAPPED BY DESIGN (TownBankCapacity.UncappableResources) -- that is why the crystal-priced magical ladders run to five figures. Cost baskets are UNCHANGED in shape: scaling never moves a resource across the WO-947 regular/magical line. NOTE the knock-on: BuildTimerConfig.TierForCost derives build TIME from the authored basket, so this pass also lifts the time ladder -- which is the intended coupling (see that file: \\\"the whole ladder re-tunes itself for free when the JSON cost pass lands\\\").\",\r\n \"_firstStepRule\": \"v38 = WO-1217 SLICE A  -  THE FIRST UPGRADE STEP IS A RULE, NOT A HAND-AUTHORED ROW. OWNER RULING 2026-08-26, verbatim: \\\"would take hours just to level anything in the start\\\". \u2b50 THE RULE: repo.upgradeCost[0] (the L1->L2 rung) == round(repo.cost[r] * 1.5) FOR EVERY RESOURCE r, on every entry that authors an upgradeCost array. It was a flat x3 of the build cost on all four towers (Archer Tower L2 = 1080 wood / 480 iron, which at WO-1216's ~37 wood per wave is ~29 waves for ONE rung) and x7.5 on mine_crystal. Archer L2 is now 540 / 240  -  the owner's own number. \u26d4 ONLY THE FIRST RUNG IS FLATTENED: upgradeCost[1..] (L3 and beyond, including the six-level storage ladders) keep their ECONOMY SINK PASS values VERBATIM, so the ladder still climbs steeply and a maxed structure stays a real commitment  -  only the first rung stops being a wall. \u26d4 APPLIED BY FORMULA ACROSS ALL 10 ROWS THAT AUTHOR AN ARRAY, IN ONE PASS  ",
