er at L1, _L2 at L2, _L3 at L3 (Assets/StructureContent/Tower_Wooden_Watchtower{,_L2,_L3}.fbx, each with a sibling .fbx.tripo",
            "-extracted marker proving Tripo authorship). ART RE-POINT ONLY: stable id, gameplay stats, cost, footprint, heightMul 1.2 (the cadence anchor) and saved placements are all unchanged. SUPERSEDED HISTORY, KEPT NOT DELETED (CLAUDE.md section 15) -- 2026-09-01: \\\"owner rejected the wooden-watchtower look. Archer Tower uses the prior castle ladder again: Round at L1, Square at L2, Medieval Big at L3.\\\" That 09-01 line named the Polyperfect castle prefabs (Assets/polyperfect/Low Poly Ultimate Pack), which are NOT the owner's art; the 09-02 ruling reverses it.\",\r\n   \"visualPrefabPath\": \"Structures/Tower_Wooden_Watchtower\",\r\n   \"repo\": {\r\n    \"behaviorId\": \"DefenseTower\",\r\n    \"buildCost\": 400,\r\n    \"cost\": {\r\n     \"wood\": 360,\r\n     \"food\": 0,\r\n     \"iron\": 160,\r\n     \"crystals\": 0\r\n    },\r\n    \"maxLevel\": 3,\r\n    \"upgradeCost\": [\r\n     {\r\n      \"wood\": 540,\r\n      \"food\": 0,\r\n      \"iron\": 240,\r\n      \"crystals\": 0\r\n     },\r\n     {\r\n      \"wood\": 3150,\r\n      \"food\": 0,\r\n      \"iron\": 1400,\r\n      \"crystals\": 0\r\n     }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"upgradeVisualPath\": [\r\n     \"Structures/Tower_Wooden_Watchtower_L2\",\r\n     \"Structures/Tower_Wooden_Watchtower_L3\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"preservePrefabRotation\": false,\r\n    \"_preservePrefabRotationNote\": \"STAYS FALSE under the 2026-09-02 wooden-watchtower re-point, and the reason changed -- read it before flipping it. All three Tripo watchtower prefabs bake their Tripo X correction on the CHILD FBX instance, not on the prefab ROOT (measured off the .prefab YAML this session: L1 m_LocalRotation w 0.7187333 / x -0.69528586, L2 w 0.7071068 / x -0.7071068, L3 w 0.7071068 / x +0.7071068, all on the nested instance whose parent is the identity root). VisualFactory.Skin's identity reset only touches the CLONE ROOT, so the baked child upright survives with this flag false. Setting it true would preserve a root that is already i