            "amage\": 6,\r\n    \"fireRate\": 2.5,\r\n    \"canHitAir\": false,\r\n    \"element\": \"None\",\r\n    \"projectileStyle\": \"bolt\",\r\n    \"placement\": {\r\n     \"mustSitOn\": \"Ground\",\r\n     \"footprint\": 1.75,\r\n     \"noOverlap\": true,\r\n     \"checkAffordable\": true\r\n    },\r\n    \"upgradeTexturePath\": [],\r\n    \"_upgradeTextureNote\": \"Left EMPTY on purpose under the 2026-09-02 wooden-watchtower re-point. Each Tripo tier prefab already carries its own authored materials (Tower_Wooden_Watchtower.mat, Tower_Wooden_Watchtower_L2_part_0..8.mat, Tower_Wooden_Watchtower_L3.mat, all beside the FBXs in Assets/StructureContent/), so no per-tier texture override is needed. Do not re-add one to \\\"fix\\\" a tier that renders untextured -- that would be a material-assignment bug in the prefab, not a missing override here.\"\r\n   },\r\n   \"orientation\": {\r\n    \"corrected\": false,\r\n    \"manual\": false,\r\n    \"euler\": [\r\n     0,\r\n     0,\r\n     0\r\n    ],\r\n    \"offset\": [\r\n     0,\r\n     0,\r\n     0\r\n    ],\r\n    \"scale\": 1,\r\n    \"note\": \"Zero manual correction under the 2026-09-02 wooden-watchtower re-point: the Tripo X correction is BAKED INTO THE PREFABS on their child FBX instances (see _preservePrefabRotationNote), so the row needs no euler here and manual stays false. Player placement yaw remains authoritative.\"\r\n   },\r\n   \"canHitAir\": false\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n   \"id\": \"tower_ballista\",\r\n   \"manageFilters\": [\"DEFENSE\"],\r\n   \"manageArtKey\": \"building-ballista\",\r\n   \"displayName\": \"Ballista\",\r\n   \"description\": \"Slow, heavy bolts that also strike air.\",\r\n   \"type\": \"Tower\",\r\n   \"kind\": \"Cell\",\r\n   \"visualPrefabPath\": \"Structures/Ballista_L1\",\r\n   \"repo\": {\r\n    \"behaviorId\": \"DefenseTower\",\r\n    \"buildCost\": 600,\r\n    \"_costBasketNote\": \"WO-947 pin 4, OWNER 2026-08-14 verbatim: \\\"thats a baliista mechanical\\\". This row is REGULAR (wood + iron, NEVER crystals). The `wizard` in the id is STALE NAMING, not a classification  -  the row's own data is displayName 'Ballista', element None, projectileStyle 'bolt', behaviorId 'DefenseTower', per the owner rename ruling 2026-07-0",
            "8 recorded in its orientation.note. The former crystals (70 / 84 / 175) were folded 1:1 into IRON so every basket TOTAL and the tier-monotonic ladder are unchanged (160 / 192 / 400); only the composition moved. Numbers stay owner-tunable. MIRRORED in CatalogBootstrap.RegisterFallback (BuildEconomyRegression gate 12 [fallback-parity] enforces).\",\r\n    \"cost\": {\r\n     \"wood\": 240,\r\n     \"food\": 0,\r\n     \"iron\": 400,\r\n     \"crystals\": 0\r\n    },\r\n    \"maxLevel\": 3,\r\n    \"upgradeCost\": [\r\n     {\r\n      \"wood\": 360,\r\n      \"food\": 0,\r\n      \"iron\": 600,\r\n      \"crystals\": 0\r\n     },\r\n     {\r\n      \"wood\": 2100,\r\n      \"food\": 0,\r\n      \"iron\": 3500,\r\n      \"crystals\": 0\r\n     }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"upgradeVisualPath\": [\n     \"Structures/Ballista_L2\",\n     \"Structures/Ballista_L3\"\n    ],\n    \"upgradeOrientationEuler\": [\n     [90, 0, 0],\n     [90, 0, 0]\n    ],\n    \"_upgradeVisualNote\": \"WO-1046 asked whether the tower upgrade is 'just a reskin'; for this row it was not even that - maxLevel was already 3 with a two-step upgradeCost table, but there was NO upgradeVisualPath at all, so all three levels rendered the SAME borrowed wizard tower. The ladder was real in cost and stats and invisible to the player, which is the worst of both: paid for, never seen. Owner ruling 2026-08-17: 'i want it like Archer Tower - Lv2 -Lv3'. Wired to the owner-purchased Ballista_L1/L2/L3 set, mirroring tower_archer's authoring exactly. NO upgradeTexturePath: unlike the archer L3 (WO-928 defect B) each Ballista level is a SEPARATE model carrying its own basecolor, so there is no scraped-material problem to correct and a forced albedo would only override art that is already right.\",\r\n    \"navSurface\": \"Blocker\",\r\n    \"heightMul\": 0.75,\r\n    \"range\": 22,\r\n    \"damage\": 30,\r\n    \"fireRate\": 0.5,\r\n    \"canHitAir\": true,\r\n    \"element\": \"None\",\r\n    \"projectileStyle\"