            " silhouette  -  OWNER RULING 2026-08-23. It was typed Tower on the 1.2 tower cadence anchor, and STRUCTURE_ORIENTATION_FAIL flagged it 'NOT STANDING' (upright aspect 0.70 L1 / 0.94 L2, below the measured 1.2 floor). The oracle names exactly two ways to be there and they have different fixes: (a) the model is mis-oriented, or (b) the ROW is mis-classed. The owner ruled (b): a ballista is a wide machine on a carriage, so its heightMul belongs in the SIEGE-ENGINE group at 0.75 alongside tower_catapult and tower_siege_tower. \u26d4 This is a RECLASS, not a widened floor  -  the row stops failing because it is correctly classed. Do NOT widen the oracle's 1.2 tower floor to accommodate it, and do NOT 're-orient' the art: the model was never lying down. `type` stays Tower because that field is a LIVE SAVE KEY and a behaviour selector (it still fires); only the height cadence moved.\"\r\n   },\r\n   \"orientation\": {\r\n    \"corrected\": false,\r\n    \"manual\": true,\r\n    \"euler\": [\r\n     90,\r\n     0,\r\n     0\r\n    ],\r\n    \"offset\": [\r\n     0,\r\n     0,\r\n     0\r\n    ],\r\n    \"scale\": 1,\r\n    \"note\": \"X +90, MEASURED THROUGH THE REAL PLACEMENT PATH (WO-1157, owner F8 2026-08-24: 'the ballista builds on its side'). THE AXIS-BAKE RETIREMENT OF 2026-08-18 WAS WRONG ON THIS ROW AND ITS OWN REASONING IS WHY: it zeroed the euler because bakeAxisConversion:1 is set on the source FBX, i.e. it concluded from a FLAG that the mesh must arrive standing. The flag says the bake was REQUESTED; it does not say the mesh came back upright. DeNelle.Editor.BallistaPlacementProbe ran StructureFactory.Create on this row beside three controls and captured the numbers (Builds/ballista-probe.log): Ballista_L1.fbx native pose euler=[90,0,0] measures 1.002w x 0.549h x 0.702d, and the SAME asset forced to identity measures 1.002 x 0.702 x 0.549 - Y and Z swapped, which is the model lying on its face. VisualFactory applies DEF-232's identity reset to the clone root, so with this euler at zero the placed ballista shipped at identity: on its side, exactly as reported. TH",
            "E FAMILY IS THE PROOF, not this row alone: jeweler, barracks, workshop, forge and armorer are the same Tripo import family, ALL carry bakeAxisConversion:1, ALL author euler [90,0,0], and the owner has confirmed every one of them stands correctly in town - jeweler measured native aspect 1.372 upright vs 0.619 at identity in the same run. The ballista was the one row of that family left at zero. Do NOT re-zero it, and do NOT reach for repo.preservePrefabRotation instead: that flag is what StructureOrientationOracle A1(b) accuses when a preserved root carries a tilt, and this root carries 90 degrees of it - the euler channel is the one this family uses. HISTORY: was [-90,0,0] before 2026-08-18, then [0,0,0]; the sign is +90 because that is the asset's own native pose, measured, not inferred. manual:true is kept so no auto-baker re-tips the row. The LIVE structure orientation channel is entry.orientation here, applied by StructureFactory.Create when manual==true.\"\r\n   },\r\n   \"canHitAir\": true,\r\n   \"note\": \"WO-989: id renamed tower_wall_wizard->tower_ballista; alias on CatalogRegistry.Get.\",\r\n   \"_artNote\": \"SUPERSEDED 2026-08-17. Read as: 'the Ballista renders as WizardTower_1 because renaming the art was deferred.' That deferral lasted long enough that a row named Ballista, costing wood+iron, firing bolts, shipped to players showing a WIZARD TOWER - and the note describing the placeholder made it look accounted-for rather than broken. Resolved by owner-purchased art, not a rename: visualPrefabPath is now Structures/Ballista_L1 with a real L2/L3 ladder above it. Kept, not deleted, so nobody re-derives the WizardTower_1 path as current. HISTORY: WO-989 noted the path was GUID-stable and deferred the art.\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n   \"id\": \"tower_siege_tower\",\r\n   \"manageFilters\": [\"DEFENSE\"],\r\n   \"manageArtKey\": \"building-sky-ballista\",\r\n   \"displayName\": \"Sky Ballista (Anti-Air)\",\r\n   \"_heightNote\": \"SIEGE-ENGINE group, 0.75 (3.0 m), kept in the 2026-08-05 cadence pass. This one is also the only mustSitOn WallWalk row: it sits ON",
