"DEFENSE\"],\r\n   \"manageArtKey\": \"building-wooden-palisade\",\r\n   \"displayName\": \"Wooden Palisade\",\r\n   \"description\": \"Cheap timber barrier that slows attackers.\",\r\n   \"_heightNote\": \"2026-08-05 cadence pass: DELIBERATELY LEFT on the 1.0 base (4.0 m) even though a palisade reading at house height is the obvious next thing to low",
            "er. heightMul is a UNIFORM scale, so dropping it narrows the wall by the same factor - and every wall in an already-saved town sits on the cell pitch of its OLD claim, so a narrower segment does not re-pitch its neighbours, it opens pathable GAPS in existing runs and shrinks the NavMeshObstacle with it. That is a save-compat break, not a visual tweak. Lowering walls needs a measured StructureHeightAudit run (to state the before/after cell claim) plus a save-migration decision first. See the top-level _heightCadence.\",\r\n   \"_wo948Note\": \"WO-948 (owner ruling 2026-08-10): walls BUILD at L1 (wood) ONLY -- higher tiers exist only by UPGRADING the placed wall, CoC model. maxLevel capped 3->2: the ONE reachable rung is wood->stone (upgradeCost[0] is its price); the old second rung's cost row was REMOVED rather than left dormant -- steel/spiked are WO-904's behind raid-steal and must not be pre-built. upgradeVisualPath[0] swaps a L2 wall to the stone model (walls.json meshStraight paths are kaykit SOURCE paths, not runtime-loadable; the catalog row is the runtime mesh authority). wallTierBase omitted = 0 (wood is the walls.json base rung).\",\r\n   \"type\": \"Wall\",\r\n   \"kind\": \"Cell\",\r\n   \"visualPrefabPath\": \"Structures/Wall_Medieval_Wood\",\r\n   \"repo\": {\r\n    \"behaviorId\": \"WallSegment\",\r\n    \"buildCost\": 160,\r\n    \"cost\": {\r\n     \"wood\": 80,\r\n     \"food\": 0,\r\n     \"iron\": 0,\r\n     \"crystals\": 0\r\n    },\r\n    \"maxLevel\": 2,\r\n    \"upgradeCost\": [\r\n     {\r\n      \"wood\": 120,\r\n      \"food\": 0,\r\n      \"iron\": 0,\r\n      \"crystals\": 0\r\n     }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"upgradeVisualPath\": [\r\n     \"Structures/Wall_Medieval_Stone\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"navSurface\": \"Blocker\",\r\n    \"placement\": {\r\n     \"mustSitOn\": \"Ground\",\r\n     \"footprint\": 2.1,\r\n     \"noOverlap\": true,\r\n     \"checkAffordable\": true\r\n    }\r\n   },\r\n   \"orientation\": {\r\n    \"corrected\": false,\r\n    \"manual\": false,\r\n    \"euler\": [\r\n     0,\r\n     0,\r\n     0\r\n    ],\r\n    \"offset\": [\r\n     0,\r\n     0,\r\n     0\r\n    ],\r\n    \"scale\": 1,\r\n    \"note\": \"prefab 'polyperfect/Wall_Wood_Horizontal_3",
            "x3m' not found  -  no correction computed\"\r\n   }\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n   \"id\": \"wall_stone\",\r\n   \"manageFilters\": [\"DEFENSE\"],\r\n   \"manageArtKey\": \"building-stone-wall\",\r\n   \"displayName\": \"Stone Wall\",\r\n   \"description\": \"Sturdy stone barrier that holds attackers.\",\r\n   \"_heightNote\": \"2026-08-05 cadence pass: LEFT on the 1.0 base for the same save-compat reason as wall_wood - see that row's _heightNote and the top-level _heightCadence.\",\r\n   \"_wo948Note\": \"WO-948 (owner ruling 2026-08-10): PALETTE-LOCKED (build-categories.json Walls lockedIds) -- walls build at L1 wood only; stone is reached by upgrading a placed wood wall. This ROW SURVIVES so existing saves replay/sell placed stone walls (BaseLayoutLoader resolves via CatalogRegistry, which never consults the palette). maxLevel 3->1: a legacy placed stone wall already sits AT the stone rung; deeper rungs (steel/spiked) are WO-904's behind raid-steal, so its upgradeCost table was removed. wallTierBase 1 = its walls.json ladder level (Stone) -- the WallDefense heart-mitigation derive reads it.\",\r\n   \"type\": \"Wall\",\r\n   \"kind\": \"Cell\",\r\n   \"visualPrefabPath\": \"Structures/Wall_Medieval_Stone\",\r\n   \"repo\": {\r\n    \"behaviorId\": \"WallSegment\",\r\n    \"buildCost\": 360,\r\n    \"cost\": {\r\n     \"wood\": 120,\r\n     \"food\": 0,\r\n     \"iron\": 240,\r\n     \"crystals\": 0\r\n    },\r\n    \"maxLevel\": 1,\r\n    \"wallTierBase\": 1,\r\n    \"navSurface\": \"Blocker\",\r\n    \"placement\": {\r\n     \"mustSitOn\": \"Ground\",\r\n     \"footprint\": 2.1,\r\n     \"noOverlap\": true,\r\n     \"checkAffordable\": true\r\n    }\r\n   },\r\n   \"orientation\": {\r\n    \"corrected\": false,\r\n    \"manual\": false,\r\n    \"euler\": [\r\n     0,\r\n     0,\r\n     0\r\n    ],\r\n    \"offset\": [\r\n     0,\r\n     0,\r\n     0\r\n    ],\r\n    \"scale\": 1,\r\n    \"note\": \"prefab 'polyperfect/Wall_Medieval_Stone' not found  -  no correction computed\"\r\n   }\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n   \"id\": \"gate_stone\",\r\n   \"manageFilters\": [\"DEFENSE\"],\r\n   \"manageArtKey\": \"building-stone-gate\",\r\n   \"displayName\": \"Stone Gate\",\r\n   \"description\": \"Opens for you; blocks enemies until it falls.\",\r\n   \"_height",
            "Note\": \"2026-08-05 cadence pass: LEFT on the 1.0 base. A gate must stay flush with the wall run it interrupts, so it moves ONLY when wall_wood/wall_stone move - and those are blocked on a save-migration decision (see wall_wood's _heightNote).\",\r\n   \"type\": \"Gate\",\r\n   \"kind\": \"Cell\",\r\n   \"visualPrefabPath\": \"Structures/Gate_Medieval_Medium\",\r\n   \"repo\": {\r\n    \"behaviorId\": \"Gate\",\r\n    \"buildCost\": 480,\r\n    \"cost\": {\r\n     \"wood\": 240,\r\n     \"food\": 0,\r\n     \"iron\": 200,\r\n     \"crystals\": 0\r\n    },\r\n    \"navSurface\": \"Blocker\",\r\n    \"placement\": {\r\n     \"mustSitOn\": \"Ground\",\r\n     \"footprint\": 2.8,\r\n     \"noOverlap\": true,\r\n     \"minDistanceFromGate\": 8,\r\n     \"checkAffordable\": true\r\n    }\r\n   },\r\n   \"orientation\": {\r\n    \"corrected\": false,\r\n    \"manual\": false,\r\n    \"euler\": [\r\n     0,\r\n     0,\r\n     0\r\n    ],\r\n    \"offset\": [\r\n     0,\r\n     0,\r\n     0\r\n    ],\r\n    \"scale\": 1,\r\n    \"note\": \"prefab 'polyperfect/Gate_Medieval_Medium' not found  -  no correction computed\"\r\n   }\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n   \"id\": \"mine_crystal\",\r\n   \"manageFilters\": [\"ECONOMY\"],\r\n   \"manageArtKey\": \"building-crystal-mine\",\r\n   \"displayName\": \"Crystal Mine\",\r\n   \"description\": \"Yields Crystals each time a wave is cleared.\",\r\n   \"role\": \"crystal_producer\",\r\n   \"type\": \"Resource\",\r\n   \"kind\": \"Cell\",\r\n   \"visualPrefabPath\": \"Structures/CrystalMine\",\r\n   \"repo\": {\r\n    \"_crystalFaucetNote\": \"\u26d4 UNLOCKED 2026-08-24 (owner ruling, PROD-015). This is the EARLY crystal faucet and it was locked out of the Town palette, so crystals had NO town source at all - they arrived only from raids and one-time drops. Owner, verbatim: \\\"the only crystal faucet is way past when you need them, by then you are onto dungeons and raids\\\". \u2b50 AND IT IS THE RIGHT FAUCET BECAUSE OF ITS COST: wo