r (the owner-purchased Armourer model) per the same 2026-08-17 ruling that fixed the forge row. \u26a0 ORIENTATION: this is the ONE row of the set changing art FAMILY - Polyperfect prefabs are authored Y-up, Tripo FBXs are Z-up, so this row's orientation (currently ",
            "manual:false, euler 0,0,0) is now wrong where forge/jeweler/tower_ballista already carry manual:true euler -90,0,0. LEFT UNCHANGED ON PURPOSE: the owner is setting these live in Offset Forge, and authoring -90 in both places WOULD compose to 180 - upside down, not merely sideways, which is the exact WO-928 failure recorded on the archer tower row. RESOLVED 2026-08-17 BY OBSERVATION, NOT BY READING CODE (owner, on a live Play session: 'they match' / 'look good too'): with -90 authored in BOTH systems for forge/jeweler/tower_ballista, every model stands upright - so the two DO NOT COMPOSE, one wins, and the duplicate value is harmless. This row's manual:false is therefore fine as it stands: it takes its correction from Offset Forge, which is the system that is demonstrably in effect. Recorded so nobody 'fixes' the asymmetry later and reintroduces the double-apply the warning was guarding against.\",\r\n   \"visualPrefabPath\": \"Structures/armorer\",\r\n   \"repo\": {\r\n    \"behaviorId\": \"GameplayBuilding\",\r\n    \"npcModel\": \"CraftPixPeople/NPC_CityDweller_2\",\r\n    \"singleton\": true,\r\n    \"bakedTwins\": [\r\n     \"Forge_Armor_Storefront\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"buildCost\": 520,\r\n    \"cost\": {\r\n     \"wood\": 240,\r\n     \"food\": 0,\r\n     \"iron\": 280,\r\n     \"crystals\": 0\r\n    },\r\n    \"navSurface\": \"Blocker\",\r\n    \"placement\": {\r\n     \"mustSitOn\": \"Ground\",\r\n     \"footprint\": 2.38,\r\n     \"noOverlap\": true,\r\n     \"checkAffordable\": true\r\n    },\r\n    \"restoreGoldCost\": 150,\r\n    \"_productionNote\": \"IRON PRODUCER (owner ruling 2026-08-23) - but the ROLE stays \\\"armorer\\\" because role is IDENTITY, not capability. The Armorer is BOTH the armour vendor and the iron producer, and a row claims exactly one identity; overloading role to iron_producer made two oracles correctly object that no row claimed \\\"armorer\\\" any more. Production is expressed on the FAUCET side instead: collector_forge.repo.satisfiedByStructureIds names this row, so owning the Armorer opens the iron gate. Capability, not type - ARCHITECTURE_PRINCIPLES sec.3.\"\r\n   },\r\n   \"orientation\"",
            ": {\r\n    \"corrected\": true,\r\n    \"manual\": true,\r\n    \"euler\": [\r\n     90,\r\n     0,\r\n     0\r\n    ],\r\n    \"offset\": [\r\n     0,\r\n     0,\r\n     0\r\n    ],\r\n    \"scale\": 1,\r\n    \"note\": \"owner 2026-08-19 upright X=90 flagged fixed  -  applied PRE-fit via StructureFactory.OptsFor LocalRotation (GROK_BRIEF). Was [0,0,0] after 2026-08-18 axis-bake pass that discarded the imported root rotation.\"\r\n   }\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n   \"id\": \"jeweler\",\r\n   \"manageFilters\": [\"CRAFT\"],\r\n   \"manageArtKey\": \"building-jeweler\",\r\n   \"displayName\": \"Jeweler\",\r\n   \"description\": \"Crafts jewelry.\",\r\n   \"role\": \"jeweler\",\r\n   \"type\": \"Resource\",\r\n   \"kind\": \"Cell\",\r\n   \"visualPrefabPath\": \"Structures/jeweler\",\r\n   \"repo\": {\r\n    \"behaviorId\": \"GameplayBuilding\",\r\n    \"npcModel\": \"CraftPixPeople/NPC_RichCitizen_1\",\r\n    \"singleton\": true,\r\n    \"bakedTwins\": [\r\n     \"Jeweler_Gems_Storefront\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"buildCost\": 480,\r\n    \"_costBasketNote\": \"WO-947 pin 3, OWNER 2026-08-14 verbatim: \\\"Crafting (can enbue preciouus sstones future release)\\\". The Jeweler is a CRAFTING shop, therefore REGULAR (wood + iron, NEVER crystals)  -  it TRADES in gems, it is not built of magic. \u26a0 The owner flagged that a FUTURE release may let it IMBUE precious stones; that would be a re-classification AT THAT TIME and is expressly NOT a reason to make it magical today. The former crystals (30) were folded 1:1 into IRON so the basket TOTAL is unchanged (120); only the composition moved. Numbers stay owner-tunable.\",\r\n    \"cost\": {\r\n     \"wood\": 200,\r\n     \"food\": 0,\r\n     \"iron\": 280,\r\n     \"crystals\": 0\r\n    },\r\n    \"navSurface\": \"Blocker\",\r\n    \"placement\": {\r\n     \"mustSitOn\": \"Ground\",\r\n     \"footprint\": 2.38,\r\n     \"noOverlap\": true,\r\n     \"checkAffordable\": true\r\n    }\r\n   },\r\n   \"orientation\": {\r\n    \"corrected\": true,\r\n    \"manual\": true,\r\n    \"euler\": [\r\n     90,\r\n     0,\r\n     0\r\n    ],\r\n    \"offset\": [\r\n     0,\r\n     0,\r\n     0\r\n    ],\r\n    \"scale\": 1,\r\n    \"note\": \"owner 2026-08-19 upright X=90 flagged fixed  -  applied PRE-fit via StructureFactory.OptsFor LocalRo",
            "tation (GROK_BRIEF). Was [0,0,0] after 2026-08-18 axis-bake pass that discarded the imported root rotation.\"\r\n   }\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n   \"id\": \"arcane-tower\",\r\n   \"manageFilters\": [\"CRAFT\"],\r\n   \"manageArtKey\": \"building-cathedral\",\r\n   \"displayName\": \"Cathedral of Magic\",\r\n   \"description\": \"Spells and magic research.\",\r\n   \"_nameConfusionNote\": \"\u26a0 THIS ID IS NOT A TOWER. id 'arcane-tower' displays 'Cathedral of Magic' and is THRAIN'S LEVELING BUILDING (behaviorId GameplayBuilding, singleton, spells + magic research). The DEFENSIVE wizard tower is a different row: 'tower_arcane_spire', displayed 'Arcane Spire', behaviorId ArcaneTower. So the id that says tower is not one, and the one that BEHAVES as ArcaneTower is named Spire - which is why the owner asked about 'arcane tower' costs on 2026-08-24 and meant the Spire. \u26d4 IDS ARE FROZEN SAVE KEYS and cannot be renamed; only the words can move. building-tiers.json carries the same warning - it is repeated HERE because this is the file people read first.\",\r\n   \"role\": \"arcane\",\r\n   \"_costNote\": \"MAGICAL by OWNER RULING 2026-08-14, verbatim: \\\"cathedral of magic is where all magic upgrades anre and can unlock new teirs of spells\\\". WO-947 v19 folds the former wood:60 1:1 into CRYSTALS, so the basket is crystals:60 + iron:60 and the total (120) is UNCHANGED. This OVERRULES the prior reading that put this row on the REGULAR side by the jeweler analogy (\\\"a shop that DEALS IN magic is still a shop\\\"), citing repo.behaviorId 'GameplayBuilding' and the _heightNote below (\\\"despite the id this is not a tower - it is the town's one civic landmark\\\"). THE DISTINCTION: the jeweler SELLS things that happen to be precious; the Cathedral is WHERE MAGIC UPGRADES LIVE AND WHERE NEW SPELL TIERS UNLOCK - the ENGINE of magical progression, not a vendor that deals in it. 'behaviorId: GameplayBuilding' describes its BEHAVIOUR (it is not a firing tower), NOT its cost class, and the id/_heightNote say nothing about what it is MADE of. The surface evidence points both ways on purpose; the owner's",
            " ruling is the tiebreak. Do not re-litigate, and do not restore wood here - CostBasketSeparationRegression [applied] now pins this row MAGICAL with total 120.\",\r\n   \"_heightNote\": \"LANDMARK APEX, kept at 1.25 (5.0 m) in the 2026-08-05 cadence pass while the tower class came DOWN to the owner-ruled 1.2. Despite the id this is not a tower - it is a GameplayBuilding, the town's one civic landmark - and the ruling's 'relatively the same size, doesn't have to be exact' allows exactly one biggest thing. It is now the tallest structure in town by 0.05x, which is the intent. Do not re-align it to 1.2 and do not raise the towers to meet it. NORMALIZED 2026-08-06 (owner F8 flag: 'why is the cathedral of magic so large? Normalize'). Was 1.25 - a deliberate landmark-tier exception I made in the cadence pass so it would read as the tallest thing in town. Overruled: it is a GameplayBuilding despite the tower-ish id, so it sits at the 1.0 building base with the rest of the family.\",\r\n   \"type\": \"Resource\",\r\n   \"kind\": \"Cell\",\r\n   \"visualPrefabPath\": \"Structures/arcane tower\",\r\n   \"visualTexturePath\": \"Structures/ArcaneTower_Albedo\",\r\n   \"repo\": {\r\n    \"behaviorId\": \"GameplayBuilding\",\r\n    \"npcModel\": \"CraftPixPeople/NPC_RichCitizen_3\",\r\n    \"singleton\": true,\r\n    \"bakedTwins\": [\r\n     \"ArcaneTower_MagicUpgrades\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"buildCost\": 560,\r\n    \"cost\": {\r\n     \"wood\": 0,\r\n     \"food\": 0,\r\n     \"iron\": 240,\r\n     \"crystals\": 240\r\n    },\r\n    \"navSurface\": \"Blocker\",\r\n    \"heightMul\": 1,\r\n    \"placement\": {\r\n     \"mustSitOn\": \"Ground\",\r\n     \"footprint\": 8.4,\r\n     \"noOverlap\": true,\r\n     \"checkAffordable\": true\r\n    }\r\n   },\r\n   \"orientation\": {\r\n    \"corrected\": false,\r\n    \"manual\": true,\r\n    \"euler\": [\r\n     -90,\r\n     0,\r\n     0\r\n    ],\r\n    \"offset\": [\r\n     0,\r\n     0,\r\n     0\r\n    ],\r\n    \"scale\": 1,\r\n    \"note\": \"owner hand-dialed 2026-06-21 via HubStructureVisualInjector swap table (sizeM 12 -> footprint fit, pitch -90, texPath forced -- FBX material lost its map link); ported WO-707 -- manual:true so no tool ove",
            "rwrites it. Swap posY -0.6 sink intentionally dropped: ReseatCorrectedBottom pins the corrected base to the placement ground (owner 2026-07-04 base-on-ground rule)\"\r\n   },\r\n   \"canHitAir\": true\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n   \"id\": \"tower_arcane_spire\",\r\n   \"manageFilters\": [\"DEFENSE\"],\r\n   \"manageArtKey\": \"building-arcane-spire\",\r\n   \"displayName\": \"Arcane Spire\",\r\n   \"description\": \"Casts Aether bolts at ground and air foes.\",\r\n   \"_upgradeCurveNote\": \"\u26a0 SUPERSEDED IN PART 2026-08-26 (WO-1217 Slice C  -  see _wo1217CrystalGateNote): the build/L2 crystal numbers below (200 / 400) are RETIRED  -  build and L2 cost NO crystals at all. Only the L3 800 still stands, and the iron figures below (160 / 480 / 1400) are also superseded by 360 / 540 / 1400. Kept for the reasoning, not for the numbers. \u26d4 CRYSTAL CURVE RE-RULED 2026-08-24 by the owner: 200 / 400 / 800 (build / L2 / L3), replacing 200 / 1500 / 4370. Her reasoning, verbatim: \\\"to get 5 of those towers would take a year\\\". The old curve was 7.5x then 22x the entry price, so a single maxed Spire cost 6,070 crystals and five cost 30,350 - against a resource that until the same day had NO town producer at all. The new curve is a clean doubling: one maxed Spire is 1,400 and five are 7,000. \u26a0 IRON IS DELIBERATELY UNCHANGED (160 / 480 / 1400) because the owner ruled the CRYSTAL numbers only. That leaves iron the larger constraint at L3, which is arguably correct - crystals gate ENTRY, iron gates SCALE, and iron has a producer - but it is a consequence of this edit rather than a decision, and is flagged for the owner rather than silently rebalanced.\",\r\n   \"_wo1217CrystalGateNote\": \"\u26d4 CRYSTALS GATE TIER 3 ONLY  -  OWNER RULING 2026-08-26 (WO-1217 Slice C, verbatim: \\\"i think only tier 3 should cost crystals on the arcane tower\\\"). Build and L2 are now CRYSTAL-FREE; L3 keeps its 800 crystals untouched. The build basket's 200 crystals were folded 1:1 INTO IRON (160 -> 360), so the build basket TOTAL is UNCHANGED at 360  -  the same discipline the WO-947 v18/v19 conversions used. L2 then",
            " follows the v38 first-step rule (_firstStepRule): 540 iron = 1.5x the new 360 build cost, replacing 480 iron + 400 crystals. \u2b50 WHY THIS IS NOT TASTE: PROD-015 is still OPEN  -  there is no crystal faucet in town  -  so that L2 Upgrade button could not be satisfied by PLAYING at all, at any grind rate. The owner hit exactly that on device (Seeker build 2026.08.26.341419). Gating crystals to the top tier makes the Spire playable today and turns crystals into the final-tier ask, which is what PROD-015 is about. \u26a0 THIS PARTIALLY RE-OPENS WO-947 AND THE OWNER MUST BE TOLD, NOT AN IMPLEMENTER: CostBasketSeparationRegression [applied] asserts every MAGICAL basket carries NON-ZERO crystals and freezes this row's totals at 360/880/2200. The build total still reads 360, but build and L2 now carry ZERO crystals and L2 totals 540, so that suite goes RED until its AppliedRows entry is amended with these numbers AND its magical-basket rule is relaxed from 'every basket is crystal-based' to 'crystal-based AT ITS TOP TIER'. Recorded here so the precedence is explicit: the 2026-08-26 ruling post-dates the 2026-08-14 pin-1 pairing and wins on the lower two tiers; the PAIRING itself (crystals + iron, never wood) is untouched  -  no wood entered this row. \u26a0 'arcane-tower' ('Cathedral of Magic', flat 240 iron / 240 crystals, no maxLevel) is DELIBERATELY UNTOUCHED: it has no tier ladder at all, so \\\"only tier 3\\\" cannot apply to it. Whether its flat crystal cost should also move is an OPEN OWNER QUESTION (WO-1217 Slice C name-ambiguity block). Do not change it on inference.\",\r\n   \"_nameConfusionNote\": \"\u26a0 THIS is the DEFENSIVE wizard tower - behaviorId ArcaneTower - even though it is displayed 'Arcane Spire'. Do NOT confuse it with id 'arcane-tower', which displays 'Cathedral of Magic' and is a leveling building, not a defence. \u2b50 It is also the ONLY tower priced in crystals (200 as of 2026-08-24, down from 500 by owner ruling PROD-015); every other defensive tower is wood + iron. \u26a0 AND IT IS CURRENTLY LOCKED out of the Defense palette",
            " (build-categories.json), so its cost is visible while the tower is not buildable - the same shape as the iron and crystal producers found the same day.\",\r\n   \"type\": \"Tower\",\r\n   \"kind\": \"Cell\",\r\n   \"visualPrefabPath\": \"Structures/ArcaneSpire_1\",\r\n   \"visualTexturePath\": \"Structures/ArcaneSpire_Albedo\",\r\n   \"repo\": {\r\n    \"_crystalCostNote\": \"\u26a0 SUPERSEDED 2026-08-26 (WO-1217 Slice C  -  see _wo1217CrystalGateNote): the build cost is now ZERO crystals (the 200 folded 1:1 into iron). This note's own closing warning  -  \\\"when the crystal faucet lands, re-judge this number\\\"  -  was answered the other way: the faucet did not land, so the ask moved to tier 3. \u26d4 500 -> 200 CRYSTALS, owner ruling 2026-08-24 (PROD-015): \\\"it takes a long time to get 500 crystals\\\". The price was not wrong in isolation - it was unreachable, because NOTHING IN TOWN PRODUCES CRYSTALS. mine_crystal (a real working producer, behaviorId CrystalMine, maxLevel 3) is locked out of the Town palette and the Cathedral has not yet absorbed the role (WO-1168 section 4, unbuilt), so crystals arrive only from raids and one-time sources. \u26a0 SAME SHAPE AS THE IRON DEAD END the owner hit the same morning, one tier up: the game pricing something in a resource the town cannot make. \u26a0 WHEN THE CRYSTAL FAUCET LANDS, RE-JUDGE THIS NUMBER - 200 is priced against a world with no producer, and a producer changes what it is worth.\",\r\n    \"behaviorId\": \"ArcaneTower\",\r\n    \"buildCost\": 800,\r\n    \"_costBasketNote\": \"WO-947 pin 1, OWNER 2026-08-14 verbatim: \\\"Crystals and Iron\\\". This row is MAGICAL beyond doubt from its own data (element 'Aether', behaviorId 'ArcaneTower', projectileStyle 'spell'); only the PAIRING was unpinned. Basket is now CRYSTALS + IRON  -  WOOD REMOVED. The former wood (40 / 48 / 100) was folded 1:1 into CRYSTALS (the crystal side, because the ruling calls magical structures crystal-BASED) so every basket TOTAL and the tier-monotonic ladder are unchanged (165 / 198 / 412); only the composition moved. Numbers stay owner-tunable. MIRRORED in Cata",
            "logBootstrap.RegisterFallback (BuildEconomyRegression gate 12 [fallback-parity] enforces).\",\r\n    \"cost\": {\r\n     \"wood\": 0,\r\n     \"food\": 0,\r\n     \"iron\": 360,\r\n     \"crystals\": 0\r\n    },\r\n    \"maxLevel\": 3,\r\n    \"upgradeCost\": [\r\n     {\r\n      \"wood\": 0,\r\n      \"food\": 0,\r\n      \"iron\": 540,\r\n      \"crystals\": 0\r\n     },\r\n     {\r\n      \"wood\": 0,\r\n      \"food\": 0,\r\n      \"iron\": 1400,\r\n      \"crystals\": 800\r\n     }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"upgradeVisualPath\": [\r\n     \"Structures/ArcaneSpire_2\",\r\n     \"Structures/ArcaneSpire_3\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"upgradeTexturePath\": [\r\n     \"Structures/ArcaneSpire_2_Albedo\",\r\n     \"Structures/ArcaneSpire_3_Albedo\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"navSurface\": \"Blocker\",\r\n    \"heightMul\": 1.2,\r\n    \"range\": 16,\r\n    \"damage\": 20,\r\n    \"fireRate\": 0.6,\r\n    \"canHitAir\": true,\r\n    \"element\": \"Aether\",\r\n    \"projectileStyle\": \"spell\",\r\n    \"aoeRadius\": 6,\r\n    \"slowSeconds\": 2.5,\r\n    \"splashFraction\": 0.7,\r\n    \"placement\": {\r\n     \"mustSitOn\": \"Ground\",\r\n     \"footprint\": 2.1,\r\n     \"noOverlap\": true,\r\n     \"checkAffordable\": true\r\n    }\r\n   },\r\n   \"orientation\": {\r\n    \"corrected\": false,\r\n    \"manual\": true,\r\n    \"euler\": [\r\n     0,\r\n     0,\r\n     0\r\n    ],\r\n    \"offset\": [\r\n     0,\r\n     0,\r\n     0\r\n    ],\r\n    \"scale\": 1,\r\n    \"note\": \"manual  -  owner 2026-07-08 'needs 0 0 0' (local overlay save 01:47Z agrees): after the Tripo extraction reimport ArcaneSpire_1 stands natively; the earlier (-90,90,90) double-rotated it. manual=true kept so the auto baker never re-tips it.\"\r\n   },\r\n   \"canHitAir\": true\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n   \"id\": \"collector_farm\",\r\n   \"manageFilters\": [\"ECONOMY\"],\r\n   \"manageArtKey\": \"building-quarry\",\r\n   \"displayName\": \"Quarry\",\r\n   \"description\": \"Extracts Stone for your town over time.\",\r\n   \"role\": \"stone_producer\",\r\n   \"_quarryNote\": \"OWNER RULING 2026-09-05, verbatim: \\\"quarry pays stone\\\" and \\\"the farm was retired nothiong uses food, was replaced by stone which actually has uses\\\". THIS ROW IS THE QUARRY AND IT PAYS STONE. Food is RETIRED as a yield because nothing consumes it - do not autho",
            "r a replacement food producer; that is a separate owner decision, not a gap to fill. STOP - THE ID DOES NOT MOVE: 'collector_farm' is a LIVE SAVE KEY (everBuiltStructureIds, BaseLayout records, repo.bakedTwins, repo.collectorBuildingId 'farm', and the PlayerPrefs level key behind ResourceBuildingState) and the game is live on the Solana dApp Store, so renaming it orphans every existing town. Only the ROLE and the RESOURCE moved; the same law keeps HarvestResource.Food in code as the frozen persisted STONE wallet slot - ResourceBuildingProgression.LabelFor is the ONE place that turns that stored value into the player's word ('Stone'), so a HarvestResource.Food site in C# is a STONE site, never a bug to 'fix'. WO-1416 also closed the reason one building answered in three words: this row already said role 'stone_producer' while the only C# constant said 'food_producer' - a role NO row claimed - so the tile fell back to the generic 'Building' and the NPC label fell back to the retired proper noun 'Farm'; and the harvest tick printed the raw enum name ('Food') instead of putting the SAME value through LabelFor like the welcome-back popup does ('Stone'). The constant is now StructureRole.StoneProducer and the tick reads LabelFor. Pinned by CollectorIncomeRegression case 16 [quarry-pays-stone].\",\r\n   \"_heightNote\": \"1.4 IS NOT A CADENCE OUTLIER - DO NOT NORMALIZE IT TO 1.0. That half of the original note was right and it STANDS. What it MISSED is the other axis, and that is what the owner finally felt on 2026-08-20 ('farm seems to be much larger than anything else'): heightMul is a UNIFORM scale, so it moves the FOOTPRINT by the same factor it moves the height, and this model's fitted pose is FLAT. MEASURED on device, not theorised (logs/device/2026-08-20-portal.log, [Flow:Xform] + [Flow:VisualFactory] 'skinned'): Structures/farm is natively 0.977 x 1.000 x 0.391 m, and this row's orientation euler (-90,0,0) stands the 0.391 axis UP, so Fit divided the 5.6 m target (4 m base x 1.4) by 0.391 and produced scale=(14.34) an",
            "d a fitted footprint of 14.00 x 14.34 m - against a family that measures 2.8-5.8 m across. That is 3.5x, and NO value of heightMul fixes it: lowering it re-ships the shrunk farm (commit 31b41d19), raising it makes the footprint worse. THE CORRECTION IS repo.maxFootprint 5.6 (added 2026-08-20) - a footprint CEILING that scales the fitted model DOWN uniformly until its widest horizontal extent is 5.6 m, the same number as this row's placement.footprint, so the visual and the collision claim finally agree. Final rendered size 5.47 x 2.19 x 5.60 m; the grid claim shrinks 5x5 cells -> 2x2, which is overlap-safe for saved towns. WHY THE OLD MECHANISM READ WRONG, kept so nobody re-derives it: 'the windmill blades inflate this model's Y bounds' is not what the geometry says - the art is a flat square plot, not a spindly silhouette - but the old note's CONCLUSION was correct for the pipeline it was written against. Until the GROK_BRIEF change of 2026-08-19 the euler was applied AFTER the fit, so Fit measured the UNROTATED 1.000 axis, 1.4 yielded scale 5.60, and the farm rendered at exactly 5.47 x 2.19 x 5.60 - the size the owner accepted. Moving the euler PRE-fit flipped which axis Fit divides by, and only this row's art is flat enough for that to matter. The cap value is chosen to reproduce that owner-accepted size in BOTH regimes: under the old order the widest extent is 5.60 and the cap is exactly non-binding, under the current order it binds and lands on the same numbers - so this row can no longer be resized by a change to rotation ORDER. heightMul 1.4 is deliberately KEPT and is INERT while the cap binds (any heightMul above ~0.55 lands on the same capped size); it remains the documented fallback if the cap is ever disarmed. If it ever needs retuning, retune the CAP against the rendered body standing next to a forge, never against the number.\",\r\n   \"type\": \"Collector\",\r\n   \"kind\": \"Cell\",\r\n   \"visualPrefabPath\": \"Structures/farm\",\r\n   \"repo\": {\r\n    \"behaviorId\": \"ResourceCollector\",\r\n    \"npcModel\": \"CraftPixPeople",
